{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers","id":1530163,"title":"Doppelgangers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-07T08:07:37-08:00","id":1530163,"title":"Doppelgangers","content":"Ok, NPC appears, very traumatized, may be lacking a soul, may think they are dead. Has been reliving their murder/death over and over again, as someone tried to create doppelgangers...<br /> <br /> What does your cabal do? <br /> <br /> What kind of Mage/Necromancer/Slasher would do such a thing, could the very well become a Deviant? <br /> <br /> What if the escape from this torture was only possible because the doppelgangers consumed each other, eventually becoming more powerful than their creator/captor? <br /> <br /> So now you have an angry, high rank ghost to deal with...<br /> <br /> (This scenario is based on recent conversation about Death twilight and castoffs, wherein I realise it is easy to create unlimited rank 0 castoffs, but that means if you create a Deny the Reaper style way of bringing someone back, and the repeatedly kill them, you could create an unlimited number of doppelgangers, each more traumatized than the last...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:20:51-08:00","id":1530173,"title":"","content":"First would be getting a Mind mage nearby, or an imbued item that recharges Willpower, in order to delay the progress of Soulessness to Enervation. Second would be reporting to the Sentinel asap, there is reasonable doubt a Reaper walks the Consilium. After that, use Space magic to try to find the soul and see if an Eleventh Question is available, since time is of the essence. <br /> <br /> After the Reaper steals the soul, they figured they could get some powerful contacts and supernatural favors by using this process to provide a steady supply of ghosts for Eaters of the Dead. Alternatively, they could be interested in blending all of them into a gestalt and making them merge with the empty vessel, probably as part of an Obsession about the nature of Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T14:41:20-08:00","id":1530206,"title":"","content":"As an aside, i ask myself how interesting or not would be the doppelgangers and the process of their making to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cult_of_the_Red_Word\" target=\"_blank\">Red Word</a> members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T15:20:58-08:00","id":1530211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530206#post1530206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, i ask myself how interesting or not would be the doppelgangers and the process of their making to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cult_of_the_Red_Word\" target=\"_blank\">Red Word</a> members.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What you call history is nothing but a dead timeline, Anchored to the Fallen World, drinking from the lifeblood of possibility and infecting it, like a mosquito. <i>The Dead Belong Below</i>, the Underworld hungers, see what happens when he had the feverish delirium thorn from his eyes, when he realizes his soul <a href=\"https://paulocoelhoblog.com/2013/05/15/the-well-of-madness/\" target=\"_blank\">drank from the waters of madness</a>, how he struggles even now to throw off the toxin. We must allow this delusion of history to fade, we must let it go and let the waters of the Ocean of Fragments grant it a merciful end. Find the Red Words of the Prince, they are the lifeblood of history renewed.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-07-2024, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T17:47:57-08:00","id":1530227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530173#post1530173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First would be getting a Mind mage nearby, or an imbued item that recharges Willpower, in order to delay the progress of Soulessness to Enervation. Second would be reporting to the Sentinel asap, there is reasonable doubt a Reaper walks the Consilium. After that, use Space magic to try to find the soul and see if an Eleventh Question is available, since time is of the essence.<br /> <br /> After the Reaper steals the soul, they figured they could get some powerful contacts and supernatural favors by using this process to provide a steady supply of ghosts for Eaters of the Dead. Alternatively, they could be interested in blending all of them into a gestalt and making them merge with the empty vessel, probably as part of an Obsession about the nature of Sin-Eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind Mage is able to hold the willpower at bay, but suggests putting our poor victim (J. Doe) to sleep as their mental anguish seem quite bad.<br /> <br /> The Sentinel asks would you to give up Doe or if you would prefer to take the lead on the investigation.<br /> <br /> The best student of Space conclude that there is no soul with a sympathy to Doe, either it is shielded or gone. He's not sure if it has passed on or if someone has veiled the connection to appear that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> If there is a reaper they are hiding their tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T18:32:04-08:00","id":1530232,"title":"","content":"I imagine if this is an NPC that unless anyone more experienced intervenes, the cabal would want to investigate. Putting them in a dreamless sleep might help.<br /> <br /> But before that, apply Occam's Razor, see if its possible (without violating the Veil) to ask the NPC for permission to investigate further. See if there are any suspicious emails, weird books, unusual cards, weird residue on their clothes, ask people they knew, etc. Maybe do a Streetwise check for anything that would catch the NPC's eye, a scam that could be supernatural, or ask a savvy mage (maybe a Guardian).<br /> <br /> On the supernatural side, some ideas that come to mind:<br /> <br /> Did the Mind mage find any memories that could be scrutinized or a location that could be examined with <i>Postcognition </i>?<br /> <br /> What did Focused Death Sight reveal ? Did the dopplegangers remember anything ?<br /> <br /> If we have the aid of a good combatant, have them with us and then cast <i>Shifting the Odds</i> for &quot;soul thief&quot; (need to think this one through very carefully).<br /> <br /> If we are at a loss, there is always <i>Serendipity</i>.<br /> <br /> In case all the above fails and a crazy idea is better than no idea: Were they sure this isn't a red herring, someone made with <i>Create Life</i> with conjunctional Mind ?<br /> <br /> <b>Observation:</b> There is always the possibility that the Reaper is a long standing member of the Consilium, in which case <i>Pierce Deception </i>and <i>Supernal Veil</i> could reveal withheld information. But its worth avoiding the type of paranoia that can burn bridges, unless things escalate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T19:45:25-08:00","id":1530240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers#post1530163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(This scenario is based on recent conversation about Death twilight and castoffs, wherein I realise it is easy to create unlimited rank 0 castoffs, but that means if you create a Deny the Reaper style way of bringing someone back, and the repeatedly kill them, you could create an unlimited number of doppelgangers, each more traumatized than the last...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the assumption that I'm reading your supposition correctly: A Doppelganger is specifically the ghost of a person formed from circumstances that don't kill them, and those are the types of ghosts-of-the-same-people who benefit from gaining Rank from consuming their fellows, while <i>every</i> ghost of the same person erodes the other through physical contact by virtue of counting as a Bane for them.<br /> <br /> Also, much as you wouldn't expect a new spirit of a river to emerge while the existing one is still around (or a new Goetia of the same concept to be formed in a person's Oneiros while you've got it bound out in the material world), I'd imagine getting a bunch of Doppelgangers would entail some <i>variety</i> in the life-altering trauma and near-death experiences, to say nothing of how the mechanics of Doppelgangers being written for a game where holding death at bay is far from commonplace and comes with costs and limits and therefore it is probably unwise to assume you can torture a godlike ghost out of someone in unexceptional circumstances.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that this is going to be an <i>extremely haunted person</i> subjected to <i>extremely turbulent times</i> as part of a <i>very involved scheme</i> that probably <i>concludes with</i> their death. Possibly some esoteric torture to cultivate Phantom Limbs to feed the original Doppelganger, maybe throw in an outside attempt to give the resulting non-geist ghost a Key through Deathmasks or a captured geist or one of those recurring pipe dreams people have of stealing water from the Rivers, or maybe they're just sticking with the efficiencies question of how big a mass of ectoplasm you can get out of a single person.<br /> <br /> If this results in a Deviant it's almost certainly not because of anything to do with Awakened magic, because the Remade condition doesn't work that way \u2014 more variables than torture and death go into cracking a soul open to precipitate Scars and Variations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T01:04:37-08:00","id":1530253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530240#post1530240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the assumption that I'm reading your supposition correctly: A Doppelganger is specifically the ghost of a person formed from circumstances that don't kill them, and those are the types of ghosts-of-the-same-people who benefit from gaining Rank from consuming their fellows, while <i>every</i> ghost of the same person erodes the other through physical contact by virtue of counting as a Bane for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is usually how a doppleganger is formed. But if you simply kill them and then bring them back to life, that is a sufficiently traumatic experience that I think it would create a ghost at least some of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, much as you wouldn't expect a new spirit of a river to emerge while the existing one is still around (or a new Goetia of the same concept to be formed in a person's Oneiros while you've got it bound out in the material world), I'd imagine getting a bunch of Doppelgangers would entail some <i>variety</i> in the life-altering trauma and near-death experiences, to say nothing of how the mechanics of Doppelgangers being written for a game where holding death at bay is far from commonplace and comes with costs and limits and therefore it is probably unwise to assume you can torture a godlike ghost out of someone in unexceptional circumstances. </div> </div> </div> oh this is definitely unwise. The issue with dopplegangers is that they demonstrate it IS possible to create multiple ghosts of the same person. The question is how, and what impact the soul (or lack there of) has.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm saying is that this is going to be an <i>extremely haunted person</i> subjected to <i>extremely turbulent times</i> as part of a <i>very involved scheme</i> that probably <i>concludes with</i> their death. </div> </div> </div> Yes. This is so messed up, which is why I'm assumed, if their soul is even remotely intact, they could end up becoming a Deviant, but I haven't read Deviant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly some esoteric torture to cultivate Phantom Limbs to feed the original Doppelganger, maybe throw in an outside attempt to give the resulting non-geist ghost a Key through Deathmasks or a captured geist or one of those recurring pipe dreams people have of stealing water from the Rivers, or maybe they're just sticking with the efficiencies question of how big a mass of ectoplasm you can get out of a single person. </div> </div> </div> I think if I was running a cross-over Geist game with ectoplasm as plasm I would limit the plasm per day that a Mage can create from their body to their health levels, and from a corpse to it's corpus (not per day, but per corpse)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this results in a Deviant it's almost certainly not because of anything to do with Awakened magic, because the Remade condition doesn't work that way \u2014 more variables than torture and death go into cracking a soul open to precipitate Scars and Variations. </div> </div> </div>How about multiple deaths? I don't know what the requirements are, but I fear a Mage who decides to try and find out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T05:07:35-08:00","id":1530264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530253#post1530253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is usually how a doppleganger is formed. But if you simply kill them and then bring them back to life, that is a sufficiently traumatic experience that I think it would create a ghost at least some of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying I'm pretty sure dying creates a normal ghost even if the person is then restored to life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> oh this is definitely unwise. The issue with dopplegangers is that they demonstrate it IS possible to create multiple ghosts of the same person. The question is how, and what impact the soul (or lack there of) has. </div> </div> </div>If you have the proficiency in Death to Deny The Reaper you have the capacity to create a ghost based on an existing person without even doing anything to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think if I was running a cross-over Geist game with ectoplasm as plasm I would limit the plasm per day that a Mage can create from their body to their health levels, and from a corpse to it's corpus (not per day, but per corpse) </div> </div> </div>Plasm and ectoplasm are explicitly the same thing, per the same book that establishes Fate as the Arcanum needed to see qashmallim in Twilight. I was referring to the prospect of seeing how &quot;large&quot; a ghost one could make from a single person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. This is so messed up, which is why I'm assumed, if their soul is even remotely intact, they could end up becoming a Deviant, but I haven't read Deviant. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about multiple deaths? I don't know what the requirements are, but I fear a Mage who decides to try and find out. </div> </div> </div>The Divergence is generally a process that doesn't have a more stable and established supernatural framework attached to it like those found in other gamelines. There's a reason Deviant is a) one of the &quot;these can occur by accident&quot; types of monster, b) used to model an extremely wide variety of phenomena only unified by their basis in damaging the soul and its spiritual consequences, and c) built on the assumption that mortals are the primary drivers and antagonists the Remade deal with.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say that if nothing more unusual than using Awakened magic to resurrect a person is involved in the situation, becoming a Deviant would pretty much by necessitate be because there was something unusual about that person. (And keeping the soul in the body past the moment of death so it's still there to break open would itself make Paradox from the spell to revive them the more likely avenue of complication.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Clarifying the ectoplasm line. 02-08-2024, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T09:05:12-08:00","id":1530282,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> ni first, Thanks, this is a really interesting storytelling exercise for me to build on a simple idea/mystery, I'm hoping to run a one-shot or a series of one-shots. It is especially nice when players don't know the setting very well to be able to prompt them with ideas that their characters should know (like contacting the Sentinel, which wouldn't have occurred to me). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530232#post1530232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine if this is an NPC that unless anyone more experienced intervenes, the cabal would want to investigate. Putting them in a dreamless sleep might help. But before that, apply Occam's Razor, see if its possible (without violating the Veil) to ask the NPC for permission to investigate further. See if there are any suspicious emails, weird books, unusual cards, weird residue on their clothes, ask people they knew, etc. Maybe do a Streetwise check for anything that would catch the NPC's eye, a scam that could be supernatural, or ask a savvy mage (maybe a Guardian).</div> </div> </div> </div> I definitely assume the PCs would want to investigate. The NPC is in a terrible state, like a rank 1 ghost, barely intelligible, you can ask, or maybe try going into his memories or Onerios. Searching them mundanely seems reasonable, I wonder if that is the first thought that PC mages would have. Suspicious items, I suspect the antagonist would have ignored the possibility that someone would look for such items (and not bothered to remove them/hide their tracks) pretty much for the same reason I don't think Mages would jump to searching for them. A blind spot for mundane solutions (plus being fairly low wisdom) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the supernatural side, some ideas that come to mind: Did the Mind mage find any memories that could be scrutinized or a location that could be examined with Postcognition ? </div> </div> </div> Postcognition or searching their memory will reveal a repeated scene of them painfully dying, before being brought back, sometimes days in between, sometimes minutes. The deaths are gruesome but I don't think it is necessary to go into details (partly because i don't feel comfortable with it and partly because i haven't come up with them) but it is the same death each time. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What did Focused Death Sight reveal ? Did the dopplegangers remember anything ? </div> </div> </div> Likewise, the dopplegangers (if and when you find them) will likely mostly be rank 1/0 ghosts barely able to remember or do much more than re-enact the death scene (or consume each other). Focussed Death sight is an interesting question. I don't know, looking at the rules, active Mage (Death) Sight will show the person being an Anchor for several ghosts (the doppelgangers which the players may not have encountered yet). And it will reveal the fact that our Doe has no soul. Focused Mage Sight will reveal surface information, like yes, this is Supernal, the Death Arcana was involved, and a signature Nimbus will be revealed, along with likely a timeline of weeks of repeated exposure to whatever caused this. And probably locked beneath some opacity I would give hints that it is a practice of Unmaking. I don't know what to say for deep information. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we have the aid of a good combatant, have them with us and then cast Shifting the Odds for &quot;soul thief&quot; (need to think this one through very carefully). </div> </div> </div> In this case, this will lead them down a wild goose chase, as the soul wasn't stolen. But the spell will still find them a soul thief (at which point i might just retcon things so I didn't have to come up with new plot). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we are at a loss, there is always Serendipity. </div> </div> </div> Serendipity could lead them to some member of the consillium higher status member, someone with connections who would recognise the signature Nimbus if asked. Or lead them to the &quot;kill room&quot; where they may meet a very angry ghost, possibly rank 4/5. Or hmm... Serendipity could be very strong, wondering how vague it should be, or open to interpretation... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In case all the above fails and a crazy idea is better than no idea: Were they sure this isn't a red herring, someone made with Create Life with conjunctional Mind ? </div> </div> </div> Yes, the focused magic sight will reveal that this is Death not Life/Mind linked. Not sure how else they would get this info though (or what the opacity should be, partly because tooling for scrutiny isn't that much fun, so I have never used the rules for scrutinizing). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Observation: There is always the possibility that the Reaper is a long standing member of the Consilium, in which case Pierce Deception and Supernal Veil could reveal withheld information. But its worth avoiding the type of paranoia that can burn bridges, unless things escalate. </div> </div> </div> Pierce Deception and Supernal Veil?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T09:14:50-08:00","id":1530283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530264#post1530264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying I'm pretty sure dying creates a normal ghost even if the person is then restored to life.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is the dopplegangers are basically normal ghosts except that the person is still alive. And that all ghosts from the one person have this bane/absorbtion feature regardless of whether one was created when they died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have the proficiency in Death to Deny The Reaper you have the capacity to create a ghost based on an existing person without even doing anything to them. </div> </div> </div>This would be temporary rather than lasting, and not sure what would happen if two such artificial ghost merged, or one merged with a doppleganger.... Would be less convinced how it should work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plasm and ectoplasm are explicitly the same thing, per the same book that establishes Fate as the Arcanum needed to see qashmallim in Twilight. I was referring to the prospect of seeing how &quot;large&quot; a ghost one could make from a single person. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, plasm being ectoplasm is only an issue in cross-over games where unlimited Plasm from a Mage is suddenly far more valuable.<br /> <br /> With Making is there a limit to the size attributes you could create limits only by the scale or the spell? Or would a Patterning effect alter the size of a pre-existing ghost again to the limit of the scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T10:39:52-08:00","id":1530287,"title":"","content":"<i>Pierce Deception</i> and <i>Supernal Veil </i>would be in case the person responsible is an investigator or in case someone high ranking is covering for them. So you use them to discern lies while talking to them, while simultaneously not triggering their Peripheral Mage Sight. But there are lots of reasons they could be lying, dangerous information that needs to be redacted (&quot;We secretly have a Logophage to erase knowledge of the Yellow Sign and avoid having a gulmoth pulling an SCP-2440&quot;), a need to be careful not to make the culprit more active, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Serendipity</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Upon casting, the mage receives a clear omen that suggests a course of action that will lead her closer to her goal. This seldom guarantees immediate success, especially if the task before her is complicated, but can provide an important breakthrough.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So it seems the caveat is that it needs to move them closer to their goal, minimalistically a waypoint on their journey and opening a new avenue for investigation, like a clue that helps recontextualize their perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Shifting the Odds</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;An Apprentice of Fate always has access to what she needs at the moment. The mage focuses on locating a particular kind of person, place, or thing, and this spell directs her steps to it unerringly as soon as possible within the next 24 hours as long as the spell remains active. Casting the spell looking for a kind of person in a crowd or an item anywhere it could appear is usually enough to immediately succeed.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on that interpretation, it seems like a wild goose chase is outside of its purview. Maybe a soul thief could teleport into town, but I think this is one of those situations where it might be a good idea to talk to the players rather than bring in a new antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:16:16-08:00","id":1530294,"title":"","content":"Ah you mean it wouldn't find a Soul Thief if none existed, whereas i was assuming a possible (but otherwise unknown) soul thief.<br /> <br /> Like maybe you end up locating the Heirarch, but have no evidence that she is a soul thief and otherwise assume the spell failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:13:00-08:00","id":1530302,"title":"","content":"I think your Hierarch example nailed it, sorry for the confusion. If there wasn't a soul thief in town, maybe one makes a stop or arrives on business, rather than the spell failing. Alternatively, like you mentioned, locate the Hierarch and the learn they are a soul thief, although maybe not who you expected to locate. I think you get a feel for when you meet the person summoned by the spell, but I don't remember where that is mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T04:24:07-08:00","id":1530361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1530163-doppelgangers?p=1530264#post1530264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying I'm pretty sure dying creates a normal ghost even if the person is then restored to life.<br /> <br /> If you have the proficiency in Death to Deny The Reaper you have the capacity to create a ghost based on an existing person without even doing anything to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>geist2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple Doppelg\u00e4ngers: Multiple ghosts of the same individual always count as one another\u2019s Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>So ghost or doppelganger, from the same person, all counts as each other's bane.<br /> <br /> The wording here doesn't seperate out the way the person died as making doppelgangers somehow different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Curiously, when two ghosts formed from the same person touch, they merge, the weaker of the two destroyed and consumed as essence by the stronger </div> </div> </div>Here again, doppelganger and ghosts formed from the same person are used interchangeable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...These stories all describe the ghosts the Bound call Doppelg\u00e4ngers. </div> </div> </div>Here suggests that doppelgangers aren't metaphysically different from other ghosts, they are just called something different because the person they come from is still alive.<br /> <br /> So my reading of:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ectophagia: A Doppelg\u00e4nger who fully consumes another ghost of the same person gains 1 Rank. </div> </div> </div>Is &quot;A ghost who fully consumes another ghost of the same person* gains 1 rank&quot;<br /> <br /> Ghost of the same person is equivalent to saying doppelganger, this is consistent with the fluff quoted above (though it says the two just have to touch and the weaker is destroyed and consumed... Whereas both being each other's bane and the ectophagia rules make it seem much more traumatic and uncertain which one will come out on top.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that, like the only way of gaining rank (ie drinking from the rivers of the Underworld) a doppelganger is changed by the experience, consuming something of another ghost means their memories are merged and they become one in some sense.<br /> <br /> But since they both come from the same person that change will not he as significant, ie more memories of the same person makes them more whole in some sense, rather than losing personality and becoming more aligned to the Underworld (ie no keys/other changes which happen to a Geist).<br /> <br /> Specifically, absorbing a phantom limb would mean the ghost would restore their body to not having a missing limb (so if you died years after losing a limb, a ghost would be able to restore that limb if they found the phantom limb before it got absorbed by the Underworld...) - though in this case I would be skeptical about granting an additional rank for absorbing a single rank 0 limb...<br /> <br /> NB: I also have questions about abmortals, and if they leave ghosts/doppelgangers when they are die but come back.<br /> <br /> I think for most of them I would lean towards no.<br /> <br /> Assuming the criteria of &quot;dies and comes back&quot;<br /> Bloodbathers ? not applicable?<br /> Body thieves ? Not applicable?<br /> The Purified - No, they have become spirits which do not leave ghosts when they die and come back - may have one ghost from the ritual? Maybe for the ritual to be successful it must somehow transform the one ghost into a spirit and thus they would only have doppelgangers from before becoming Purified.<br /> <br /> Eternal - feels like a no but maybe.<br /> <br /> The way they anchor themselves to an item makes them feel like a ghost already, in which case they don't really die, like the Purified. But I am leaning towards possible creation of doppelgangers everytime they would die as it is a traumatic event.<br /> <br /> Reborn - these are the most interesting, the question is , would ghosts from subsequent reborn lives be &quot;from the same person&quot;. It is pretty explicit that their soul acting as a vessel which passes on. I suppose if we consider a ghost to be a vital part of the soul (carrying the memories - which reborn explicitly retain) then the would leave no ghosts.<br /> <br /> But I tend to think of ghosts/doppelgangers as Fragments of the left overs, memories shatters not mere copies. The soul normally sheds those memories when a person dies and leaves the ghost behind (to be consumed by the Ocean of Fragments and pass on?) This could definitely be different in the reborn. So I think I am going to come down as a solid maybe.<br /> <br /> Patchwork people: N/A?<br /> <br /> Edit: sorry, to be clear, my thesis is, Doppelgangers are normal ghosts.<br /> <br /> Normal ghosts can absorb each other and gain rank, but only if they are from the same person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":".  clarification . 02-09-2024, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T08:36:10-08:00","id":1530449,"title":"","content":"I think of doppleganger as being created when a moment resonates with death at such a personal, emotional level that it imprints a snapshot in Twilight.<br /> <br /> The Reborn add the memories of their previous lives atop their current ones. While they are theoretically the most likely to have big personality changes, they are still the same person. So their dopplegangers might look like their current form and may behave vastly different, but still qualify for merger. What kind of ghost results from that absorption is a question in itself, maybe one that looks closer to the original life as the Rank increases, making the situation a very confusing Mystery for an outsider.<br /> <br /> In the case of the Purified, they have died and probably their soul departed, but they still retain a connection to their humanity. So while I imagine their partial spirit nature desensitized them from mundane death and doesn't make enough of an impression to cause a doppleganger to appear, being in a situation where they barely escaped their final death could. Elder Purified are said to have spent too long in the Shadow and think closer to spirits, so they might leave an odd doppleganger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/